---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { socials } from '../config';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Akil Fernando: incoming MSc student in Computer Science at the University of Calgary, with a background in software, games, IT, and cybersecurity.">
  <header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">About / A little context</p><h1 class="display">Curiosity,<br />put to work.</h1><p class="intro-copy">I'm Akil. I build software, work with systems, and keep coming back to the question of how they could work better.</p></header>
  <section class="section-grid" aria-labelledby="background"><p class="overline">01 / The background</p><div><h2 class="display section-title" id="background">Came to it through building.</h2><div class="body-copy"><p>Software development has been a part of my life since high school. That interest took me to Dalhousie University, where I completed a <strong>Bachelor of Computer Science</strong> in 2025, with a GPA of 3.92 and recognition as a Sexton Scholar.</p><p>During my gameplay programming co-op at Ubisoft Halifax, I worked in Unity and C# on cameras, targeting, character AI, and debugging tools. Personal projects took me further down the stack into OpenGL and Vulkan. Building a renderer from scratch made the GPU a little less mysterious. It also made me appreciate everything an engine does on your behalf.</p><p>At Teams Squared, I lead IT operations and cybersecurity. That includes identity governance, endpoint security, and the organization's ISO 27001:2022 ISMS. I also build internal software: a training platform, a fleet management system, and a client portal. Real users make the tradeoffs concrete.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/career">Experience &amp; education</a></div></section>
  <section class="section-grid" aria-labelledby="next"><p class="overline">02 / What's next</p><div><h2 class="display section-title" id="next">More deliberate questions.</h2><div class="body-copy"><p>I'm an incoming MSc student in Computer Science at the University of Calgary. My proposed research, with Dr. Nimmi Weeraddana, examines bugs that require coordinated changes to source code and assets in open-source Unity games.</p><p>I want to bring the habits of building into research, then learn where intuition needs to give way to evidence. Working prototypes are a starting point. Understanding whether they help, why they help, and under what conditions is the more interesting part.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/research">Research direction</a></div></section>
  <section class="section-grid" aria-labelledby="outside"><p class="overline">03 / Outside the work</p><div><h2 class="display section-title" id="outside">Other ways of paying attention.</h2><div class="body-copy"><p>I also write fiction, play games, and keep notes on books and film. Different forms, but often the same interest in how a small choice changes the whole experience.</p><p>Some of that lives in my <a href="/writing">creative writing</a> and my <a href="/log">reading and playing log</a>. Technical reflections go in the <a href="/blog">notes</a>.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section-grid" aria-labelledby="contact"><p class="overline">04 / Contact</p><div><h2 class="display section-title" id="contact">Say hello.</h2><ul class="contact-list">{socials.map(s => <li><span>{s.label}</span><a href={s.href}>{s.handle}<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a></li>)}</ul></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .contact-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 2rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .contact-list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: 1rem; font-size: .875rem; }
  .contact-list li > span { color: var(--ink-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem; padding-top: .15rem; }
  .contact-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .contact-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  @media (max-width: 450px) { .contact-list li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .4rem; } }
</style>
